Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.18,0:00:39.58,Karaoke Translation op,TITLE,0,0,0,,{\3c&HFFFFFF&\fscx150\fscy120\c&H000000&\move(342,350,318,348,1,4380)}Space Battleship
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.73,0:00:39.58,yamato,TITLE,0,0,0,,{\c&H0000FF&\fscx347\fscy257\pos(868,926)}Yamato
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.78,0:00:39.58,Karaoke Translation op,TITLE,0,0,0,,{\3c&HFFFFFF&\fscx167\fscy142\c&H000000&\move(1490,872,1510,886,3,3840)}Soldiers of Love
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.06,0:03:06.84,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Are you alright ? Are you hurt ?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.30,0:03:08.88,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,I’m fine. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.88,0:03:09.82,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,That’s good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.38,0:03:11.82,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,I don’t know where my brother is…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.28,0:03:12.66,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Eh ?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.26,0:03:14.36,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,…or my mom…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.18,0:03:18.20,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,…or dad…!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.66,0:03:22.96,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Don't worry. They must have\N gone to the mine already.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.62,0:03:25.52,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,I’ll look for them later.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.00,0:03:26.72,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Really ?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.04,0:03:27.96,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Sure thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.26,0:03:32.56,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Now, let’s go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.44,0:03:49.28,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,What’s wrong ?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.46,0:03:52.18,def2,GILR,0,0,0,,Yamato…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.96,0:03:53.36,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Eh ?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.14,0:04:03.28,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Brother…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.64,0:04:04.16,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Huh ?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.20,0:04:32.02,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,If you’re still alive, head to the bridge !
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.36,0:05:10.98,def2,FURUHASHI,0,0,0,,Commander, this is Furuhashi,\N these Gatlantis soldiers are…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.52,0:05:30.06,def2,HIJIKATA,0,0,0,,We still have many options to continue our fight…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.74,0:05:34.24,def2,HIJIKATA,0,0,0,,…but I want to avoid further losses on both sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.92,0:05:37.10,def2,HIJIKATA,0,0,0,,We’ll surrender.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.68,0:05:38.64,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}Surrender ?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.28,0:05:40.82,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}What does surrender mean ?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.22,0:05:44.98,def2,HIJIKATA,0,0,0,,To acknowledge defeat and end a battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.98,0:05:45.70,def2,HIJIKATA,0,0,0,,You are…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.70,0:05:47.62,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}You want to end the battle ?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.62,0:05:50.10,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}Then die.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.94,0:05:58.06,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}Fight and die. \NThat will bring peace to this planet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.60,0:06:02.92,def2,HIJIKATA,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}They truly are demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.22,0:06:07.42,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,Commander Hijikata…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.46,0:06:14.63,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Fight and die ?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.48,0:06:16.63,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Fine by me !
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.63,0:06:20.10,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,But I can't involve civilians.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.30,0:06:23.64,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Use that to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.26,0:06:27.02,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,That's impossible.\N That can't carry all of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.48,0:06:30.54,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,Perhaps just the children…?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.42,0:06:37.13,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,With kids on board, we can't fly \Nwildly to break out of the enemy siege.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.68,0:06:39.68,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.68,0:06:41.80,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,That's why we have to place our bets on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.20,0:06:43.23,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Wha…?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.23,0:06:45.30,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Wait. Why me ?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.86,0:06:55.38,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Is it because I’m a woman…?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.38,0:06:58.48,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Bring a rescue ship to the pits of hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.04,0:07:01.60,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Only you can do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.26,0:07:12.74,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,You owe me, Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.44,0:07:36.02,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,I’m…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.64,0:07:48.24,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,I’m…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.06,0:08:01.02,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Go, Nagakura !
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.98,0:08:15.78,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}I'm not running away.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.82,0:08:24.06,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}I'll bring a rescue ship for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.56,0:08:59.26,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,Here's a visual of the enemy fleet just \Nbefore Warrant Officer Nagakura warped in.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.90,0:09:02.96,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,Gatlantis…
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.80,0:09:06.23,def2,NANBU,0,0,0,,It's almost like they're right on our doorstep.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.23,0:09:07.92,def2,NANBU,0,0,0,,Why didn't we notice them ?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.50,0:09:12.84,def2,OHTA,0,0,0,,I believe there's an old Garmillas \Nlogistics base on the 11th planet.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.44,0:09:20.16,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,Yeah, we’ve been developing the planet for the last 3 years, using the artificial sun we set up during the previous war.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.90,0:09:25.60,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,There must be a great number of\N Earth and Garmillas civilian settlers there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.18,0:09:29.48,def2,AIHARA,0,0,0,,The battle began more than 40 hours ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.48,0:09:31.50,def2,AIHARA,0,0,0,,Communications have been out for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.58,0:09:34.20,def2,OHTA,0,0,0,,No survivors then ?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.32,0:09:38.46,def2,TODOU,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}This is a serious matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.32,0:09:43.38,def2,TODOU,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}I didn't expect Gatlantis to\N advance to the Solar System so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.22,0:09:46.86,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Then why do you want us to stay out of this ?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.40,0:09:51.26,def2,TODOU,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}The size of the enemy is too large \Nfor the Yamato to handle by itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.00,0:09:55.66,def2,TODOU,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}I want you to continue your trip to Telezart.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.04,0:09:57.66,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,But then…
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.00,0:10:02.24,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,What about rescuing survivors ?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.00,0:10:05.58,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,We’ll do our best, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.14,0:10:08.63,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,As soon as our dialogue with Garmillas is over...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.63,0:10:12.02,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}...we'll make our move to recapture the 11th planet.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.72,0:10:23.08,def2,SHINOHARA,0,0,0,,Just pass by ?\NWe aren't going to rescue them ?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.08,0:10:26.10,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,Right.\NApparently those are HQ's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.88,0:10:33.76,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,I've heard that Garmillas has a\Nstrong influence on this expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.76,0:10:36.63,def2,SHINOHARA,0,0,0,,HQ’s worried about them ?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.63,0:10:37.90,def2,SHINOHARA,0,0,0,,No way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.90,0:10:41.32,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,{as a matter of fact}Truth be told, we have \None Gammie on the ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.50,0:10:48.82,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,With maximum acceleration, this is the \Nshortest route from our current coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.82,0:10:58.48,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,If we warp every 16 hours, the Yamato should be able to get to the zone where the message was sent in 29 days.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.62,0:11:03.64,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,As you can see, the 11th planet is way off the route.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.10,0:11:10.08,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,Since the Yamato's objective is to learn\N the truth of Teresa's message ASAP…
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.08,0:11:11.72,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,Our objective is to save lives…
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.62,0:11:15.33,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,…by responding to the message from Telezart.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.33,0:11:16.90,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,That's my understanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.86,0:11:18.72,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,H…hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.72,0:11:23.38,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,Therefore, I find it contradictory that we'd\N abandon drowning people right before our eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.92,0:11:25.08,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,I can’t accept that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.08,0:11:28.88,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,You are…
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.26,0:11:31.84,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,You saved my life, Lieutenant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.98,0:11:36.20,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,Why are you here ? \NOnly high-ranking officers are…
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.20,0:11:41.06,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,Is there any difference between Garmillas and\N Earth when it comes to saving our own people ?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.54,0:11:44.63,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,I might sound cruel, but it's been too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.63,0:11:46.34,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,There won't be any survivors.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.82,0:11:49.33,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,We won't know unless we go there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.33,0:11:50.98,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,In fact, one person escaped.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.98,0:11:54.74,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,This argument has no merit.\N I want to hear the Acting Captain’s decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.64,0:12:04.34,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,The situation makes it dangerous\N for the Yamato to charge in by itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.28,0:12:08.94,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,But that's nothing compared\N to the situation at Planet Balan.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.78,0:12:13.66,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,I’ll follow the tactics Captain Okita used back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.66,0:12:14.58,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,Kodai…
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.74,0:12:19.34,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,The warp out location is the mid-point between the artificial sun and the planet surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.74,0:12:20.76,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,That’s too risky.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.28,0:12:24.30,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,If we force the ship to warp out near the surface…
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.30,0:12:28.14,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{gravity}…the wave motion engine will be temporarily disabled because of gravity damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.66,0:12:30.33,def2,TOKUGAWA,0,0,0,,It'll take 2 hours to resume.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.33,0:12:33.18,def2,TOKUGAWA,0,0,0,,During that time, the shock cannons \Nand wave motion barrier won't…
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.86,0:12:34.94,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,I’m aware of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.34,0:12:38.74,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,Quite decisive. \NThat tactic is definitely like Okita’s.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.28,0:12:44.52,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,{sore}But the Yamato’s objective is not to retrieve dead bodies by taking such a risk, is it ?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.04,0:12:50.42,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,She escaped the battlefield against all odds.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.76,0:12:54.86,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,We can only pay that off…
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.28,0:13:00.90,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,…if we believe that there are still survivors.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.28,0:13:08.76,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,All hands, maintain Class-1 battle\N stations and prepare to warp !
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.22,0:13:12.46,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Commence the 11th planet rescue operation !
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.48,0:13:24.54,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,If we can’t rescue drowning people right before our eyes, we won’t be able to save the universe from a crisis.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.44,0:13:28.10,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,Yamamoto Akira didn't say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.78,0:13:32.48,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,That's how she sounded to me. \NProbably the others, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.52,0:13:37.16,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,So, whoever sees Teresa’s vision will become deaf ?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.54,0:13:39.13,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.13,0:13:43.70,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Or it's because we're on the Yamato.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.28,0:13:50.13,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,The Yamato currently has a serious weakness.\N It's different from the previous journey.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.02,0:13:56.40,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,You should know what it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.26,0:14:02.53,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,What do you mean ?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.26,0:14:06.60,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,As an adviser, I have to mediate the risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.12,0:14:07.98,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,Huh ?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.20,0:14:10.46,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,The Acting Captain has approved of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.90,0:14:16.36,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,You heard him. \NGuys, re-enter the call signs.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.92,0:14:20.16,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,Don't shoot down a Garmillas\N craft from behind by mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.58,0:14:21.48,def2,GUYS,0,0,0,,Roger that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.10,0:14:23.32,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,What's on your mind ?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.96,0:14:29.10,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,Since we've decided to do this, \Nlet's get it done quickly and move on.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.06,0:14:35.50,def2,SAIJO,0,0,0,,Ten seconds to warp…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.10,0:14:36.98,def2,SAIJO,0,0,0,,…nine…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.98,0:14:37.68,def2,SAIJO,0,0,0,,…eight…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.68,0:14:38.68,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,…seven…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.68,0:14:39.68,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,…six...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.68,0:14:40.68,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,...five…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.94,0:14:39.50,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\pos(970,992)}Commander…guys… {SAIJO …seven…six...five…}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.30,0:14:41.63,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\pos(950,984)}Hang in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.63,0:14:43.42,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\pos(984,990)}I'm coming back with the Yamato.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.68,0:14:41.63,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,…four…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.63,0:14:42.63,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,…three…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.63,0:14:43.63,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,…two…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.63,0:14:44.68,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,…one.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.68,0:14:45.42,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Warp !
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.68,0:14:46.40,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,Warp.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.76,0:15:13.34,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Am I…alive ?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.34,0:15:16.38,def2,WOMAN,0,0,0,,Commander !
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.98,0:15:28.62,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,This way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.20,0:15:34.00,def2,WOMAN,0,0,0,,Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.86,0:15:53.90,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Where’s the Yamato ?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.48,0:16:01.42,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Brother told me the Yamato\N can beat these guys easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.94,0:16:06.58,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,The Yamato will come for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.18,0:16:24.00,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,Gravity interference wave detected. \NA possible warp out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.54,0:16:27.63,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,It's too early for the 8th Task Force to arrive.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.63,0:16:28.54,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,Location ?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.02,0:16:31.52,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,Unable to pin point because\N it's within the planet's gravity field.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.80,0:16:35.68,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,Expand the search range and \Ninclude the surface ! Hurry !
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.10,0:16:44.26,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,Survivors confirmed.\NEliminating hostiles.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.46,0:16:52.22,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,It came.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.53,0:16:55.22,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,It really came !
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.74,0:16:57.66,def2,GIRL,0,0,0,,Yamato…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.72,0:17:06.84,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Shima, can you hover over that bridge ?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.84,0:17:10.28,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,The air current is too strong. \NI'll use the rocket anchors to stabilize.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.28,0:17:11.32,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,I'll leave it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.32,0:17:11.98,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,{You’re the man.} Nanbu.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.98,0:17:12.72,def2,NANBU,0,0,0,,Yes ?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.32,0:17:17.63,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Cooperate with the military personnel on the bridge and pick up all the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.63,0:17:18.64,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,You take charge.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.78,0:17:19.56,def2,NANBU,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.98,0:17:27.58,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Over here ! Hurry !
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.60,0:17:28.64,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,We're saved !
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.76,0:17:33.06,def2,SAIJO,0,0,0,,Enemy fleet approaching from 4 o’clock.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.58,0:17:34.78,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,So they came.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.78,0:17:36.76,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Kato, stop the advancement of the enemy fleet.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.46,0:17:39.12,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,Ignore those horseshoe crabs.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.04,0:18:04.98,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,I got you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.22,0:18:11.94,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,That bastard isn't too bad.{so shabby.}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.36,0:18:13.06,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,{\c&HEEEDB8&}Commander !
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.44,0:18:14.14,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,What’s wrong ?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.50,0:18:16.20,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,One got through.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.20,0:18:17.72,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,Alright, I’ll just…
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.72,0:18:18.50,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,It’s mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.40,0:18:38.38,def2,SAIJO,0,0,0,,Enemy destroyer approaching from behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.96,0:18:40.73,def2,NANBU,0,0,0,,All refugees are aboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.12,0:18:42.43,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Retrieve the rocket anchors.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.82,0:18:45.32,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Yamato, take off !
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.26,0:19:05.28,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,Dammit, I can't stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.04,0:19:09.70,def2,NAGAKURA,0,0,0,,Commander…
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.70,0:19:12.23,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,What the hell ? \NWhat's wrong with the Yamato ?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.23,0:19:13.13,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,Is it running away ?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.32,0:19:20.88,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,SAM launcher, fire !
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.64,0:19:27.44,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Type-3 shell, fire !
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.90,0:20:17.63,def2,SAIJO,0,0,0,,Huh ? What's this ?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.63,0:20:21.22,def2,SAIJO,0,0,0,,There's a massive dimensional distortion in orbit.{ large concentrated \Nabnormal phase shift anomaly in this area.}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.52,0:20:22.32,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,What ?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.60,0:20:32.63,def2,GOENITZ,0,0,0,,Your Majesty,{Excellency} our almighty Emperor{kaiser}, \NI have pleasure in reporting that…
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.63,0:20:38.14,def2,GOENITZ,0,0,0,,…our 8th Task Force has reached the Zol system as planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.14,0:22:03.88,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,That’s…
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.54,0:22:07.44,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,What the…?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.80,0:22:22.48,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,The Yamato…
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.48,0:22:44.17,Karaoke Translation op,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\3c&H000000&\pos(212,874)}Episode 6
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.48,0:22:44.17,Karaoke Translation op,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\3c&H000000&\pos(360,1044)}Deadly Battle on the 11th Planet
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.40,0:23:05.00,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Tawamureru yuragu tsuki no kagami
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.40,0:23:05.00,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}The reflection of the moon is blurry and capricious
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.58,0:23:17.00,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Kokoro tokasu yuubina kami no itazura
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.58,0:23:17.00,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}Graceful God's mischief mesmerizes my heart
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.00,0:23:28.46,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Uchi ni himeta awai omoide ni
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.00,0:23:28.46,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}There's a faint memory hidden within{inside}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.46,0:23:40.94,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Iki wo fukikomu no michite yukumade
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.46,0:23:40.94,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}Breathe life into it until it's full
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.94,0:23:52.72,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Hibiku anata no mune no kodou wo
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.94,0:23:52.72,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}I hear a heartbeat echoing through
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.72,0:24:02.88,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Watashi hitori janai
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.72,0:24:02.88,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}I am not alone
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.14,0:24:14.78,def2,endsong,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Saewataru sora ni inori
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.14,0:24:14.78,def2,endsong,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}I pray to the wide open sky
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.54,0:24:38.80,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\i1\c&HFFFFFF&}Atarashii ichinichi no maku ga aketeyuku
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.54,0:24:38.80,def2,ENDSONG,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&}The curtain opens on a brand new day
